# Tracker class package prefixes to delete from decompiled smali before recompiling.
# Removes entire package trees — callers will get ClassNotFoundException.
# ONLY list packages whose callers are wrapped in try/catch or loaded dynamically.
# Packages with hard static references from Edge's own <clinit> WILL crash the app.
#
# Format: smali directory prefix relative to DEX smali root (e.g. com/adjust/sdk)
# Applied to ALL decompiled DEX files during build.

# Huawei HMS — push, analytics, device ID, ads, AGConnect (China market only)
# Edge 154: kept wrappers (com/hms/push/EdgeHmsPushHelper, EdgeHmsMessageService,
# com/adjust/sdk/oaid/HmsSdkClient) reference com/huawei/hms — stripping risks the
# same NoClassDefFoundError crash as xiaomi below. Disabled for 154; the packages
# stay dormant (manifest components stripped + telemetry URLs redirected). Re-enable
# and re-test per version if the whole-class deletion is confirmed safe again.
# com/huawei/hms
# com/huawei/agconnect

# Xiaomi Push (China market only)
# Edge 154: ChromeTabbedActivity.<init> hard-references
# com/xiaomi/mipush/sdk/PushMessageReceiver — stripping these packages causes
# NoClassDefFoundError → instant crash on launch (confirmed via Pixel logcat
# 2026-09-03). Was "safe to strip" in 146. Kept now; their manifest receivers
# are still stripped and telemetry URLs redirected, so they stay dormant.
# com/xiaomi/push
# com/xiaomi/mipush

# --- UNSAFE — do NOT strip (hard references from Edge core code) ---
# com/tencent/matrix — CRASH: UmaUtils.<clinit> → AppMethodBeat (no try/catch)
# com/kwai/koom — CRASH: koom.base.b referenced from Application.onCreate (no try/catch)
# com/adjust/sdk — risky: init called early, may have hard refs
# com/microsoft/appcenter — risky: Microsoft's own SDK, likely hard-referenced
# com/google/firebase — risky: FCM integration likely hard-wired
